WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:00.935
(laughs)

00:00:00.935 --> 00:00:02.696
- I feel like I just made
out with a gingerbread man.

00:00:02.696 --> 00:00:03.790
It's delicious.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.540
(grandiose orchestral music)

00:00:17.207 --> 00:00:20.167
- I personally love Harry Potter.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.725
- I remember seeing the
cover and I was like,

00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:23.758
"I have to read this."

00:00:23.758 --> 00:00:26.614
- My relationship to Harry
Potter, I've never met the man.

00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:27.600
- I'm so excited.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.238
(laughs)

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:33.809
(mysterious orchestral music)

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.767
- This drink is beautiful.
- Holla!

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.221
- This is a tall glass of sexy right here.

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:38.372
- Oh, my gosh.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:40.279
- Oh, that's sweet.
- Yeah.

00:00:40.279 --> 00:00:41.610
- My goodness, that's so sweet.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.794
- That's the stuff.

00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:43.898
- Oh, that's good.

00:00:43.898 --> 00:00:46.068
- It's caramelly--
- Oh (beep).

00:00:46.068 --> 00:00:47.668
I mean--
- It's butterscotchy.

00:00:47.668 --> 00:00:48.712
- Just happiness in a cup.

00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:50.438
- It could use a little
more salt, I think.

00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:52.814
- Part of me wants to
say it can't be related

00:00:52.814 --> 00:00:55.893
to anything else, it's
exclusive to Harry Potter

00:00:55.893 --> 00:00:57.691
and butterbeer, but the other half of me

00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:00.120
wants to say cream soda.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.380
- I could knock back a
few of these with Dobby.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.638
- Oh, easy. (laughs)

00:01:03.638 --> 00:01:05.617
- And the other house
elves in the basement.

00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:06.563
- I could drink this every day.

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:08.218
I could have this for breakfast,
start off my day this way.

00:01:08.218 --> 00:01:09.441
(laughs)

00:01:09.441 --> 00:01:13.191
(uplifting orchestral music)

00:01:14.618 --> 00:01:16.878
- So this is the frozen one.
- Oh!

00:01:16.878 --> 00:01:19.011
- This one looks like a milkshake.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:20.850
- Well, cheers.
- Well, cheers.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.984
- If Hogsmeade had a 7-11,
this would be their slurp,

00:01:23.984 --> 00:01:26.037
or slushie or slurpie.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:26.870
- It's not as sweet.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.128
It tastes kind of a little
bit watery, dare I say?

00:01:30.128 --> 00:01:31.455
- It's sad that I wanna say this tastes

00:01:31.455 --> 00:01:32.694
like a caramel frappuccino.

00:01:32.694 --> 00:01:34.590
- Oh, better!
- But better.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.453
- The other one is also really good

00:01:36.453 --> 00:01:38.603
and it has a lot more of the creamy top.

00:01:38.603 --> 00:01:41.106
I keep on saying "creamy
top" and I'm like.

00:01:41.106 --> 00:01:42.202
(laughs)

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:45.127
- So here's the thing, so
Harry Potter almost always

00:01:45.127 --> 00:01:47.016
went back to the Muggle
world in the summers

00:01:47.016 --> 00:01:48.907
and that's when he would
want to drink this.

00:01:48.907 --> 00:01:51.139
- I wouldn't wanna know how
much sugar is in this, though.

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:53.243
- It doesn't count in Harry Potter World.

00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:54.345
- Got the ice cream headache.

00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:55.430
- Oh yeah, my throat is like (gags).

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.465
- What's the spell to get rid of that?

00:01:56.465 --> 00:01:57.907
- You can't do spells at the table.

00:01:57.907 --> 00:01:59.049
- Oh.

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:02.549
(lively orchestral music)

00:02:04.519 --> 00:02:06.337
- It's nice and warm, cheers.

00:02:06.337 --> 00:02:08.596
- This is how I imagined butterbeer, TBH.

00:02:08.596 --> 00:02:10.206
- I hope this is a
transformative of an experience

00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:11.908
as pumpkin spice latte was.

00:02:11.908 --> 00:02:12.807
(laughs)

00:02:12.807 --> 00:02:14.841
- Oh, it smells like a candle.

00:02:14.841 --> 00:02:17.847
- I feel like this is gonna
be a very hipster butterbeer.

00:02:17.847 --> 00:02:18.680
- What?

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.837
- Oh
- Holy (beep).

00:02:21.837 --> 00:02:24.574
- Whoa. (coughs)

00:02:24.574 --> 00:02:26.617
- I wanna enjoy this in private.

00:02:26.617 --> 00:02:28.681
It's just one of those, it's so good.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.163
- I feel like they melted down a waffle.

00:02:31.163 --> 00:02:34.079
- It tastes like buttered
corn on the cob, kind of.

00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:35.568
- Yeah, I disagree. (laughs)

00:02:35.568 --> 00:02:38.112
It's way better than
corn on the cob. (laughs)

00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:40.693
- This is like Christmas in a cup.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.360
- This is my perfect everything.

00:02:44.656 --> 00:02:47.451
- I don't know, I
honestly, I know I'm taking

00:02:47.451 --> 00:02:51.049
the easy road out right
here, but I cannot pick one.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:53.122
- The hot one, the frozen one.

00:02:53.122 --> 00:02:54.990
- Can you triple--
- All day every day.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.871
- The hot one is definitely my favorite.

00:02:56.871 --> 00:02:59.112
This defied all my expectations.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.121
- This one's my favorite one
'cause it's the more subtle

00:03:01.121 --> 00:03:02.054
of the tastes.

00:03:02.054 --> 00:03:03.817
- The butterbeer at the
Wizarding World of Harry Potter

00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:05.953
is everything that I dreamed it would be.

00:03:05.953 --> 00:03:07.290
Specifically the hot butterbeer.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.987
- Yes.
- Holy crap.

00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:10.472
- This was my favorite one.

00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:12.414
I just wanna bathe in this.

00:03:12.414 --> 00:03:15.610
- I would do alohomora (laughs)
and have it just floating

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.350
behind me and then hold the other two.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.850
(lively orchestral music)

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:30.024
- I think it was actually
alcoholic in the books.

00:03:30.024 --> 00:03:32.024
They were getting tipsy.

